{
  "_why": "Paths (dotted, list indexes as numbers) that may differ from the filing goldens, per cell (<lane>/<ending> or resume/<state>). Wave 3 PR B (jobs/filing.py) makes three named changes. (1) The rule for a send that raises (decided in the plan): the intent row stays and that one name is read back by hash; any exception in that read-back counts as not proven; proven, the row is marked sent and the next file is sent; not proven, the sending stops and the job holds (exit 3) as before; an update never retires the delivered chronology in an attempt where a send raised (it holds, exit 4 update_held, for the resume). (2) A name the send record says was sent or started, whose built bytes changed since, is never sent again: the job holds (exit 3) for a person to read the folder (cells rebuilt_after_send). (3) The update's numbered name for a taken name is chosen once and kept across attempts, and the read-back never drops a sent or pending row, so a resumed records-review filing never files a second numbered copy (cells resume_name_taken_after_*). Litigation and casefile already behaved this way, so their cells do not move. Clear this list once it merges.",
